#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:124
msgid "explorer.search()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:130
msgid ""
"Searches for a configuration file. Returns a Promise that resolves with a"
" [result] or with `null`, if no configuration file is found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:132
msgid "You can do the same thing synchronously with [`searchSync()`]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:134
msgid ""
"Let's say your module name is `goldengrahams` so you initialized with "
"`const explorer = cosmiconfig('goldengrahams');`. Here's how your default"
" [`search()`] will work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:137
msgid ""
"Starting from `process.cwd()` (or some other directory defined by the "
"`searchFrom` argument to [`search()`]), look for configuration objects in"
" the following places:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:138
msgid "A `goldengrahams` property in a `package.json` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:139
msgid "A `.goldengrahamsrc` file with JSON or YAML syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:140
msgid "A `.goldengrahamsrc.json` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:141
msgid ""
"A `.goldengrahamsrc.yaml`, `.goldengrahamsrc.yml`, or "
"`.goldengrahamsrc.js` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:142
msgid "A `goldengrahams.config.js` JS file exporting the object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:143
msgid ""
"If none of those searches reveal a configuration object, move up one "
"directory level and try again. So the search continues in `./`, `../`, "
"`../../`, `../../../`, etc., checking the same places in each directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:145
msgid ""
"Continue searching until arriving at your home directory (or some other "
"directory defined by the cosmiconfig option [`stopDir`])."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:146
msgid ""
"If at any point a parseable configuration is found, the [`search()`] "
"Promise resolves with its [result] \\(or, with [`searchSync()`], the "
"[result] is returned)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:147
msgid ""
"If no configuration object is found, the [`search()`] Promise resolves "
"with `null` (or, with [`searchSync()`], `null` is returned)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:148
msgid ""
"If a configuration object is found *but is malformed* (causing a parsing "
"error), the [`search()`] Promise rejects with that error (so you should "
"`.catch()` it). (Or, with [`searchSync()`], the error is thrown.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:150
msgid ""
"**If you know exactly where your configuration file should be, you can "
"use [`load()`], instead.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:152
msgid ""
"**The search process is highly customizable.** Use the cosmiconfig "
"options [`searchPlaces`] and [`loaders`] to precisely define where you "
"want to look for configurations and how you want to load them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:155
msgid "searchFrom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:157
msgid "Type: `string`. Default: `process.cwd()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:160
msgid "A filename. [`search()`] will start its search here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:163
msgid ""
"If the value is a directory, that's where the search starts. If it's a "
"file, the search starts in that file's directory."
msgstr ""

