#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:214
msgid "cosmiconfigOptions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:216
msgid "Type: `Object`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:218
msgid "Possible options are documented below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:220
msgid "searchPlaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:222
msgid "Type: `Array<string>`. Default: See below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:225
msgid ""
"An array of places that [`search()`] will check in each directory as it "
"moves up the directory tree. Each place is relative to the directory "
"being searched, and the places are checked in the specified order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:228
msgid "**Default `searchPlaces`:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:242
msgid ""
"Create your own array to search more, fewer, or altogether different "
"places."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:244
msgid ""
"Every item in `searchPlaces` needs to have a loader in [`loaders`] that "
"corresponds to its extension. (Common extensions are covered by default "
"loaders.) Read more about [`loaders`] below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:248
msgid ""
"`package.json` is a special value: When it is included in `searchPlaces`,"
" Cosmiconfig will always parse it as JSON and load a property within it, "
"not the whole file. That property is defined with the [`packageProp`] "
"option, and defaults to your module name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:251
msgid "Examples, with a module named `porgy`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:297
msgid "loaders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:299
msgid "Type: `Object`. Default: See below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:302
msgid ""
"An object that maps extensions to the loader functions responsible for "
"loading and parsing files with those extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:304
msgid ""
"Cosmiconfig exposes its default loaders for `.js`, `.json`, and `.yaml` "
"as `cosmiconfig.loadJs`, `cosmiconfig.loadJson`, and "
"`cosmiconfig.loadYaml`, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:306
msgid "**Default `loaders`:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:318
msgid ""
"(YAML is a superset of JSON; which means YAML parsers can parse JSON; "
"which is how extensionless files can be either YAML *or* JSON with only "
"one parser.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:320
msgid ""
"**If you provide a `loaders` object, your object will be *merged* with "
"the defaults.** So you can override one or two without having to override"
" them all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:323
msgid ""
"**Keys in `loaders`** are extensions (starting with a period), or `noExt`"
" to specify the loader for files *without* extensions, like "
"`.soursocksrc`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:325
msgid ""
"**Values in `loaders`** are either a loader function (described below) or"
" an object with `sync` and/or `async` properties, whose values are loader"
" functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:327
msgid ""
"**The most common use case for custom loaders value is to load "
"extensionless `rc` files as strict JSON**, instead of JSON *or* YAML (the"
" default). To accomplish that, provide the following `loaders` value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:336
msgid ""
"If you want to load files that are not handled by the loader functions "
"Cosmiconfig exposes, you can write a custom loader function or use one "
"from NPM if it exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:338
msgid "**Third-party loaders:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:340
msgid ""
"[@endemolshinegroup/cosmiconfig-typescript-"
"loader](https://github.com/EndemolShineGroup/cosmiconfig-typescript-"
"loader)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:342
msgid "**Use cases for custom loader function:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:344
msgid ""
"Allow configuration syntaxes that aren't handled by Cosmiconfig's "
"defaults, like JSON5, INI, or XML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:345
msgid "Allow ES2015 modules from `.mjs` configuration files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:346
msgid "Parse JS files with Babel before deriving the configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:348
msgid "**Custom loader functions** have the following signature:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:358
msgid ""
"Cosmiconfig reads the file when it checks whether the file exists, so it "
"will provide you with both the file's path and its content. Do whatever "
"you need to, and return either a configuration object or `null` (or, for "
"async-only loaders, a Promise that resolves with one of those). `null` "
"indicates that no real configuration was found and the search should "
"continue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:362
msgid ""
"It's easiest if you make your custom loader function synchronous. Then it"
" can be used regardless of whether you end up calling [`search()`] or "
"[`searchSync()`], [`load()`] or [`loadSync()`]. If you want or need to "
"provide an async-only loader, you can do so by making the value of "
"`loaders` an object with an `async` property whose value is the async "
"loader. You can also add a `sync` property to designate a sync loader, if"
" you want to use both async and sync search and load functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:367
msgid "A few things to note:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:369
msgid ""
"If you use a custom loader, be aware of whether it's sync or async and "
"how that aligned with your usage of sync or async search and load "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:370
msgid ""
"**Special JS syntax can also be handled by using a `require` hook**, "
"because `cosmiconfig.loadJs` just uses `require`. Whether you use custom "
"loaders or a `require` hook is up to you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:373
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:406
msgid "packageProp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:408
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Type: `string | Array<string>`. Default: `` `${moduleName}` ``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:411
msgid "Name of the property in `package.json` to look for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:413
msgid ""
"Use a period-delimited string or an array of strings to describe a path "
"to nested properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:415
msgid ""
"For example, the value `'configs.myPackage'` or `['configs', "
"'myPackage']` will get you the `\"myPackage\"` value in a `package.json` "
"like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:425
msgid ""
"If nested property names within the path include periods, you need to use"
" an array of strings. For example, the value `['configs', 'foo.bar', "
"'baz']` will get you the `\"baz\"` value in a `package.json` like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:437
msgid ""
"If a string includes period but corresponds to a top-level property name,"
" it will not be interpreted as a period-delimited path. For example, the "
"value `'one.two'` will get you the `\"three\"` value in a `package.json` "
"like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:448
msgid "stopDir"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:450
msgid "Type: `string`. Default: Absolute path to your home directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:453
msgid "Directory where the search will stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:455
msgid "cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:457
#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:476
msgid "Type: `boolean`. Default: `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:460
msgid ""
"If `false`, no caches will be used. Read more about "
"[\"Caching\"](#caching) below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:463
msgid "transform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:465
msgid "Type: `(Result) => Promise<Result> | Result`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:467
msgid ""
"A function that transforms the parsed configuration. Receives the "
"[result]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:469
msgid ""
"If using [`search()`] or [`load()`] \\(which are async), the transform "
"function can return the transformed result or return a Promise that "
"resolves with the transformed result. If using [`searchSync()`] or "
"[`loadSync()`], the function must be synchronous and return the "
"transformed result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:472
msgid ""
"The reason you might use this option — instead of simply applying your "
"transform function some other way — is that *the transformed result will "
"be cached*. If your transformation involves additional filesystem I/O or "
"other potentially slow processing, you can use this option to avoid "
"repeating those steps every time a given configuration is searched or "
"loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:474
msgid "ignoreEmptySearchPlaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:479
msgid ""
"By default, if [`search()`] encounters an empty file (containing nothing "
"but whitespace) in one of the [`searchPlaces`], it will ignore the empty "
"file and move on. If you'd like to load empty configuration files, "
"instead, set this option to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:482
msgid ""
"Why might you want to load empty configuration files? If you want to "
"throw an error, or if an empty configuration file means something to your"
" program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:485
msgid "Caching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:487
msgid ""
"As of v2, cosmiconfig uses caching to reduce the need for repetitious "
"reading of the filesystem or expensive transforms. Every new cosmiconfig "
"instance (created with `cosmiconfig()`) has its own caches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:489
msgid "To avoid or work around caching, you can do the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cosmiconfig_README.md:491
